High on the Plaine Champagne plateau, on the edge of Black River Gorges National Park, a short path leads from a car park to the Alexandra Falls viewpoint. From there you look across a valley of native forest to a waterfall dropping into the trees, and on clear days all the way down to the south coast.

It is an easy stop when driving between Chamarel and the centre of the island, and a good place to see what the island's upland forest looks like.

## Good to know

- The plateau is often misty or wet: come in the morning for the clearest view.
- Bring a layer; it is far cooler up here than on the coast.
